          deckDescription: 'Spanish 21 uses six or eight Spanish decks; each deck has 48 cards: the standard 52 less all four 10s. Suits are French (Hearts, Diamonds, Clubs, Spades). Ranks are Ace through 9 plus Jack, Queen, King; face cards count 10. No 10-spot cards exist, which shifts odds and requires different strategy from standard blackjack.',
          suitDescription: 'Four suits as in standard French deck: Hearts, Diamonds, Clubs, Spades. Suit matters for bonus payouts (e.g. suited 6-7-8 or 7-7-7 pay more; all spades 7-7-7 pays highest).',
          rankDescription: 'Stripped 48-card rank set: Ace, 2 through 9, Jack, Queen, King. Tens are removed. Ace counts 1 or 11; face cards count 10. Used for point-total comparison to 21.',
